    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Set in the heart of scenic South West Donegal, with breathtaking views over Sliabh Liag and Teelin Bay, this substantial roadside holding comprises an extensive block of high-quality land in an outstanding coastal location.\nPositioned just outside the village of Carrick, the property enjoys exceptional frontage onto the Wild Atlantic Way (R263), while the picturesque Owenwee River forms its southern boundary. The site benefits from full commercial planning permission for the development of a whiskey distillery and visitor centre, together with ancillary facilities, including a helicopter landing pad. A new commercial entrance has already been established in accordance with the approved planning permission.\nAdding further character and development potential, the existing traditional stone farm outbuildings have planning approval for comprehensive redevelopment and refurbishment.\nWith its commanding position overlooking Sliabh Liag, one of Ireland's most iconic natural attractions, and easy access to the many tourism, outdoor, and cultural amenities of South West Donegal, this exceptional property presents a rare opportunity for a wide range of tourism, hospitality, and commercial ventures."
      },
